Two types of streams:
1. generic object stream (e.g., Stream<Integer>, Stream<String>)
2. primitive streams (e.g., IntStream, LongStream, DoubleStream)

mapToObj applies on primitive stream

Streams are lazy   //invoked only when terminal operation is applied
Optional is eager  //apply transformations immediately

streams can't be apply on null values